 "text": "Hello there, how are you? You can use small bone fire starter it fits right in your pocket. Yes, they compress down small and are great for starting dry twigs. A small knife can do it too, if you' practice. Put a few in each layer, against both your sticks and your tent. A small fire on top of the tent keeps the smoke away. Put the pot on rock between the tents, and fill each pot with water before midnight. You' wake up to clear tea water and hot water for coffee. Push it down so the loops face outside and fast it with string you brought or the old cord.",
